## Why This Is Asked
This tests designing a scalable CAPA program for multi-tenant real-time pipelines with cross-region controls and regulatory considerations, not just a checklist.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence lineage and PII flags
- Region- and tenant-aware state machine
- Minimal REST API for evidence-linked CAPAs
- Per-tenant metrics and RCA templates
- Canary rollout and rollback for CDC changes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example CAPA data model (Typescript)
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  region: string;
  schemaVersion: string;
  eventId?: string;
  evidenceUrls: string[];
  traces: string[];
  timestamp: string;
  containmentStatus: 'detected'|'contained'|'mitigated'|'verified'|'closed';
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement data lineage capture across CDC and streaming layers?
- What rollback safety checks would you add to the canary plan?

## Why This Is Asked

Covers a realistic data-leak risk from IAM misconfig in pipelines, focusing on formal CAPA processes at a beginner level.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data modeling
- Lifecycle state machines
- Evidence-driven REST APIs
- Metrics for containment and prevention
- RCA templates and canary-based remediation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Express route to POST /caps
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let caps = [];
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const cap = { id: Date.now().toString(), ...req.body };
  caps.push(cap);
  res.status(201).json(cap);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you secure the CAPA API (authorization, audit logs, idempotency)?
- How would you integrate with existing incident response tools?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests CAPA fundamentals under real-world data issues: region awareness, basic data modeling, and a simple remediation flow.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model, lifecycle, REST API, regional metrics, RCA, canary.
- Trade-offs: latency of detection vs noise, data retention for evidence.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express REST endpoints
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let store = [];
app.post('/caps', (req, res)=>{ const cap={id:Date.now().toString(), ...req.body, status:'detected', created_at:new Date().toISOString()}; store.push(cap); res.status(201).json(cap);});
app.put('/caps/:id', (req,res)=>{ const idx=store.findIndex(c=>c.id===req.params.id); if(idx>=0){store[idx]={...store[idx], ...req.body}; res.json(store[idx]);} else res.status(404).end();});
app.listen(3000);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate and test the canary plan before broader rollout?
- What telemetry would you capture to ensure no regression after remediation?

